    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 1 test, 0 failures/errors).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented rejection of a future `registrationDate` on `POST /api/owners`, responding **400**, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\n**New files:**\n- `rest/escalation/FutureRegistrationDateException.java` \u2014 checked exception (extends `Exception`).\n- `rest/escalation/FutureRegistrationDateExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds `400` with `{\"error\": \"...\"}`, mirroring the existing `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler`.\n- `rest/function/owner/ValidateRegistrationDate.java` \u2014 reads the republished `@Val OwnerFieldsDto` and throws when `registrationDate` is supplied and `isAfter(LocalDate.now())`.\n- `officefloor/escalation/...FutureRegistrationDateException.yml` \u2014 wires the handler.\n\n**Modified:**\n- `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted a `validateRegistrationDate` step right after `validate` (which binds/republishes the body) and before the normalization steps.\n\nThe check is skipped when no date is supplied (it defaults to the server date via `ApplyRegistrationDate`), matching the OpenAPI spec. The new acceptance test `errorRejectsFutureDate` passes and the full build is green.",
